    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.git\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12.x\n\n### Description\n\nNot entirely sure whether this is a bug here or one in [snacks picker](https://github.com/folke/snacks.nvim).\n\nAnyway, when I open a file through snacks picker, and then try to do `Git show main:%`, I get an error message that says\n\n```\n(mini.git) fatal: path '/home/my_user/my_project/some_dir/somefile.cpp' exists on disk, but not in 'main'\n```\n\n`:pwd` in vim does correctly show project root after the snacks picker open, so it doesn't seem to come from there.\n\nThis does not happen if I either open the file directly, or if I use mini's picker.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```lua\n-- Clone latest 'mini.nvim' (requires Git CLI installed)\nvim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\nlocal mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim\"\nlocal clone_cmd = { \"git\", \"clone\", \"--depth=1\", \"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim\", mini_path }\nvim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\nvim.cmd('echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw')\n\n-- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\nvim.cmd(\"packadd mini.nvim\")\nrequire(\"mini.deps\").setup()\n\n-- Add extra setup steps needed to reproduce the behavior\n-- Use `MiniDeps.add('user/repo')` to install another plugin from GitHub\nvim.pack.add({ \"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini-git\" })\nvim.pack.add({ \"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.pick\" })\nvim.pack.add({ \"https://github.com/folke/snacks.nvim\" })\n\nrequire(\"mini.git\").setup()\nrequire(\"mini.pick\").setup()\n```\n\n1. Open a file from snacks picker in a git repo with `:lua Snacks.picker.files()`\n2. Run `:Git show main:%`",
